      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The Washington Commanders staggered through a 5-12 slog last fall, finishing third in the NFC East and six games back - a grim reminder that hope springs eternal only if you draft like you mean it. But this weekend's draft turned into a <strong>disaster ranked dead last among all 32 teams at -17.92 pick efficiency</strong>, per the sharp minds at FF Metrics, with front-office whiffs that left fans groaning louder than at a Jayden Daniels interception. They swung for edges - think athletic freaks like a speedy corner out of LSU in Round 2 and a bruising linebacker from Alabama late - but the fits felt forced, scheme mismatches in Dan Quinn's defense that scream camp cut candidates. Undrafted gems? A scrappy UDFA quarterback from Liberty scooped up quick, hinting at depth-chart chaos behind Daniels. No immediate saviors here; this class slumps toward roster bubble battles. Rookies rarely rescue rebuilds overnight - remember the bust parade of '23? - yet Quinn's mantra rings: \"Scheme sells it.\" <strong>Watch OTAs next month: if these kids mesh, redemption brews; if not, another lost autumn looms</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated May 8, 2026"
      },
